Z||000000||RobertVol||02-20-2000||03:10 PM||||With a "Fortunate" turn I have gotten from a friend at a local Buick dealer a GREAT deal and now have in my possesion a GEN II brand new 3.8 supercharged v-6. NOW ! the big question .who other than ACE does these and is there any body on THE EAST COAST ?!??!! particularly in the southeast !?!? I need to know ||||reg||6
Z||000001||stimpy||02-20-2000||03:34 PM||||Lucky you Robert!  I don't have the <BR>answer to your ? but after my dad had <BR>his sc 3.8 installed by ACE, I can <BR>tell you that you do want to look <BR>elsewhere. If you do wind up shipping <BR>your car off to have the work done, I <BR>would recommend Chris West in L.A.. <BR>He fixed most of the stuff that ACE <BR>left undone.  Are you hooking up the <BR>4 spd auto or do you have a std <BR>tranny?  My dads engine is out of a <BR>Bonniville with the auto trans, and <BR>is stuck with the ridiculous 110 mph <BR>speed limiter. Dos anyone know how to <BR>bypass this? It is one torque-y <BR>engine.  85 mph pulls about 2000 rpm. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||RobertVol||02-20-2000||06:00 PM||||This is the GEN II 3.8 designed and used in the Pontiac Grand Prix GTP. 240 HP. I have a centerforce Stage 2 in my car (5 speed) Which I believe will have enough to hold the beast with no slippage. There is no limiter on this engine. ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Oreif||02-20-2000||08:13 PM||||Since your in Florida I looked in the Fiero Yellow pages and found the following:<BR>Denny Patton 407-862-9208 Altamonte springs FL<BR>Specialty Cars Unlimited 305-726-0971 N Lauderdale, FL<BR>These are the only 2 listed for swaps in Florida or Georgia. If neither of these help You could try one of the Fiero clubs in Florida to see if they have someone they recommend.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Phil||02-20-2000||09:34 PM||||You WILL have a blast with it. Show up at Daytona in March and you can see my 3800 5sp||||reg||1
Z||000005||Guinea Pig||02-20-2000||10:03 PM||||Right now I am having a supercharged 3800 installed in a 88 formula.  Bob Steiger of   Twin Lakes Fiero<BR>1977 E. 600 North Rd<BR>Paxton, Il 60957<P>1-217-386-2669<BR>is doing the install.  I know he's not in the area you prefer, but he is considered one of the best.  He is also versatile as he is putting a Ford SHO in a Fiero for a man in one of the Carolinas.  He is doing the engineering for both the mechanicals and the body.  Very nice looking project.  He too has cleaned up messes from installs by people in Colorado and Florida.  I don't know whether he could accomplish the conversion between now and the Daytona Show (he's pushing the clock to complete mine and it's not an absolute). Hope this will be of some help.  ||||reg||1
