Z||000011||stimpy||02-24-2000||07:12 PM||||I don't have a 3.8 in mine,(just wish I did) My dad ithe one with the 3.8 from ACE. ACE sourced what they said was a zero mile motor and 4T60E from a 97 Bonniville SSEi. Per the Clutters, the Bonne was pulled directly off the line and chopped to pieces to study build quality.  Umm-hmmm, yeah, sure! I doubt that dad has put 5000 miles on the car (including driving back from CO) and just had to have the tranny rebuilt.  ACE made absolutely ZERO provision for a torque strut (aka dogbone or replacement) This is evidenced by the gouges taken out of the underside of the decklid by the alternator pulley. When he brought it home, I could take the engine by the s/c pulley and rock it back and forth 3-4"! Think what the torque of a S/C 3.8 would do! <BR>  Well, it did. In addition to the mysterious decline of the "zero mile" tranny, the exhaust system was snapped.  For some reason that I cannot recall, he had to have the blower taken off. I believe it was a gasket thing. Also the fuel pump was not upgraded as it must be.<BR>  On top of this, I had requested of the people at ACE to ship back the 2.8 that had come out of the car as  felt that it could be salvaged. They never answered my emails. Not a yes, no, or go f*** yourself.  I left messages on the answering machine. Never answered. <BR>  On the other hand, Chris West is relatively easy to get ahold of, does the work well and does not gouge on prices. He can come across as somewhat of a know-it-all, but the fact is he pretty much does know it all.  <BR>  If you do want more info on the travesty that is ACE, I would be happy to forward emails to my dad and he would happily respond. ||||reg||1
